  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 155 AM EST Sat Nov 28 2026\n\nToday-Sunday... Surface high pressure analyzed over the Gulf early \ntoday will gradually slide eastward across the Florida peninsula and \ninto the western Atlantic through Sunday. Modeled PWATs suggest a \nthin ribbon of moisture settling over central Florida early this \nweekend as a band of energy passes aloft. This moisture will \nmostly be reflected through increased mid to high level cloud \ncover, and measurable rainfall remains out of the forecast through\nat least Sunday afternoon. Another cool start is expected today \nwith temperatures mostly in the low to mid 50s near sunrise. \nToday's highs remain below normal spreading the low to mid 60s \n(north) and upper 60s to low 70s (south). Morning temperatures \nincrease a degree or two on Sunday with a more noticeable warming \ntrend through Sunday afternoon (widespread 70s) as southerly flow \nbegins to develop on the west side of the surface ridge. \nScattered showers (~20-40%) are forecast to return to the area \nSunday evening and overnight as a plume of moisture is advected \nfrom the south and the next cold front approaches central Florida.\n\nMonday-Friday... Moisture is further reinforced early next week as \nthe cold front sags into central Florida. Scattered rain chances\nare forecast Monday (~30-50%) increasing in coverage on Tuesday \n(~40-70%) before the front is pulled south of the area on \nWednesday. Surface high pressure building along the eastern seaboard\nmid week should bring a return of mostly dry conditions Wednesday\nand Thursday, although cannot rule out an occasional coastal \nshower either day. Will watch for increasing moisture again into \nFriday as high pressure moves offshore and a period of southerly \nflow redevelops. A wide temperature gradient spreads central \nFlorida Monday and Tuesday with highs in the low 70s (north) to \nupper 70s (south). A more uniform warming trend is forecast \nWednesday and into late week with highs widely ranging the low to \nmid 80s on Friday. Low temperatures in the 60s Monday morning may \nfall a few degrees across areas north of the I-4 corridor Tuesday.\nWarming low temperatures are then expected into late week, \nranging the mid 60s to low 70s by Friday morning.",
